    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight mb-4 text-white">
      C9 vs C7 Commercial Holiday Lights: Spacing &amp; Electrical Limits
    </h1>

    <p class="text-red-100 text-base sm:text-lg max-w-3xl leading-relaxed mb-6">
      The choice between <strong>C9</strong> and <strong>C7</strong> commercial lighting fundamentally dictates visual scale, roofline presence, and electrical current demands. Understanding the mechanical differences in base sizes (E17 vs E12), optimal socket spacing (12-inch vs 15-inch), and LED power consumption prevents tripping breakers and ensures professional street appeal.
    </p>

    <!-- Technical Infographic Hero Diagram -->
    <div class="bg-slate-900/80 border border-red-500/30 rounded-xl p-5 max-w-3xl">
      <h3 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-red-300 font-bold mb-3">Dimensional &amp; Photometric Specifications</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-center">
        <div class="bg-slate-950/80 p-3 rounded-lg border border-red-500/20">
          <span class="text-2xl font-black text-red-400">C9 (E17 Base)</span>
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-white mt-1">2.25-in Height &times; 1.25-in Dia</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 mt-1">Large architectural bulb; standard for rooflines and 2-story gutter eaves.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-950/80 p-3 rounded-lg border border-amber-400/40">
          <span class="text-2xl font-black text-amber-300">C7 (E12 Base)</span>
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-white mt-1">1.50-in Height &times; 0.88-in Dia</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 mt-1">Candelabra base; ideal for ground garden stakes, window frames, and railings.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-950/80 p-3 rounded-lg border border-green-500/20">
          <span class="text-2xl font-black text-emerald-300">0.58W vs 7.0W</span>
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-white mt-1">LED vs Incandescent</div>
